      "writtenOn": "2024-08-01T12:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m trying to find ways to not have to do a priority queue like this that changes the order of operations a posteriori.\n\nIf the expandResolveRect is just on D3D11, for now the two workaround don\u0027t interact, so maybe things are fine. But otherwise how would things break down if the workaround is used at the same time as the feature (and reordering doesn\u0027t happen)? I\u0027m having trouble figuring out what\u0027s the issue.",
      "revId": "f792164ef6c3c31d775b3de6f41b3bd2f4ae6ce0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "770a0935_5243faad",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/RenderPassWorkaroundsHelper.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-01T14:27:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the code again. I think PartialResolve \u0026 ResolveMultipleAttachmentInSeparatePasses\u0027 callbacks are mostly independently. They don\u0027t have to be strictly ordered. So the priority queue might be unnecessary.\n\nFor example:\n- A render pass has:\n  - attachment A:\n    - loadOp\u003dExpandResolveTexture\n    - storeOp\u003dDiscard\n    - resolveTarget\u003dA1.\n  - attachment B:\n    - loadOp\u003dLoad\n    - resolveTarget\u003dB1.\n    \nPartialResolve  splits the render pass into:\n- RP 1:\n  - attachment A:\n    - loadOp\u003dExpandResolveTexture\n    - storeOp\u003dStore\n    - resolveTarget\u003dnull \n  - attachment B:\n    - loadOp\u003dLoad\n    - resolveTarget\u003dB1.\n- RP 2:\n  - attachment A1:\n    - blit A to A1.\n- RP 3:\n  - attachment A:\n    - storeOp\u003ddiscard.\n\nResolveMultipleAttachmentInSeparatePasses splits the RP 1 into:\n- RP 1\u0027:\n  - attachment A:\n    - loadOp\u003dExpandResolveTexture\n    - storeOp\u003dStore.\n    - resolveTarget\u003dnull \n  - attachment B:\n    - loadOp\u003dLoad\n    - resolveTarget\u003dnull.\n- RP 4:\n  - attachment B:\n    - resolveTarget\u003dB1.\n    \nRP2+RP3 vs RP4 can happen in any order: RP4-\u003eRP2-\u003eRP3 or RP2-\u003eRP3-\u003eRP4. So the callbacks don\u0027t have to be strictly prioritised. I think we can keep the old code structure without priority_queue. Just place  PartialResolve above ResolveMultipleAttachmentInSeparatePasses. Its callback will be executed after the latter\u0027s but it\u0027s fine.",
      "parentUuid": "f471c498_96a18a0a",
      "revId": "f792164ef6c3c31d775b3de6f41b3bd2f4ae6ce0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
